    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1679">

                <pb facs="1066" n="950" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/697.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Nicaragua.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to our
                    conversation of to-day in regard to obtaining from Brown Brothers &amp; Company
                    and Seligman &amp; Company of New York, fifty thousand dollars ($50,000) for the
                    use of your Government, I would advise you that I have informed these bankers of
                    the contents of the memorandum which you left with me this morning, and of Mr.
                    Bryan’s autographic statement endorsed thereon. I enclose a copy of this paper
                    for your use.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
